KG42.register("rules-141fdadeb210b0e87e29ec9f",{"id":"26-battery_flexibility::v141-c-R007","paper":"26-battery_flexibility","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R007","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Market payment","process_stage":"settlement","market_meaning":"The purchasing prosumer incurs a cost and the selling peer earns money when the P2P transaction occurs. Scope: Flexi User community P2P purchases by prosumers and corresponding seller receipts. Condition: A prosumer buys electricity from a fellow peer.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function settlement.payment under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["execution.energy_trade","settlement.payment"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R007-E001","source":"settlement.payment","target":"execution.energy_trade","type":"conditional_on","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e19"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Flexi User community P2P purchases by prosumers and corresponding seller receipts.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e19"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"The purchasing prosumer incurs a cost and the selling peer earns money when the P2P transaction occurs. Scope: Flexi User community P2P purchases by prosumers and corresponding seller receipts. Condition: A prosumer buys electricity from a fellow peer.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e19"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e19","location":{"location_id":"src-9788b5496d-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.2.2 Market specific constraints","anchor_text":"u- amount someone pays and the other one earns will cancel out, we leave ir these terms out of the o","equation_id":"(6)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In the Flexi User market with decentralised storage, costs arise when a prosumer consumes from the grid or buys from a fellow peer. However, in the P2P trade, the selling peer earns money and thereby reduces the costs of electricity for the overall community. As the amount someone pays and the other one earns will cancel out, we leave these terms out of the optimisation. Thus, the objective function for this case minimises the sum of costs for grid consumption G^{(t,h)}, Eq. (6). \\min \\sum_h \\sum_t [p_G^{(t)} \\cdot G^{(t,h)}] (6)."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"No R007-specific payment, receipt, or settlement decision variable is declared in the frozen graph. The source evidence for this rule states that P2P payment and receipt amounts cancel and are omitted from the optimisation rather than being modeled as explicit settlement decision variables.","empty_theta_reason":"No R007-specific settlement price, payment coefficient, or tariff parameter is declared in the frozen graph. Although the paper defines local P2P prices elsewhere for pricing and clearing rules, the supplied R007 evidence gives no participant-level payment formula or parameter binding for settlement, so none is asserted here."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e19","quote":"In the Flexi User market with decentralised storage, costs arise when a prosumer consumes from the grid or buys from a fellow peer. However, in the P2P trade, the selling peer earns money and thereby reduces the costs of electricity for the overall community."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"c05049a767e9c9381d716af77793ec685fa05c00ef9e8870e066c0ba31434368","applicability":"needs_revision","reason":"The supplied source evidence states qualitatively that a purchasing prosumer pays and a selling peer earns, but explicitly says these P2P payment and receipt terms cancel at community level and are left out of the optimisation. It provides no participant-level settlement identity, price application, or payment/receipt variable definition for R007. Thus the existing core constraint C001 remains not_formalized; no source-supported expression can be supplied without inventing buyer/seller settlement variables or a payment formula. The frozen graph represents only the conditional relation of settlement.payment on execution.energy_trade.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","node_ids":["settlement.payment","execution.energy_trade"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"C001 describes the settlement consequence of a P2P purchase by a prosumer: the buyer incurs a payment cost and the seller receives income. The frozen edge v141-c-R007-E001 expresses the relevant condition by making settlement.payment conditional_on execution.energy_trade. No additional graph relationship or invented payment formula is asserted."}],"revision_requests":["Confirm whether R007 is intentionally a qualitative settlement-accounting rule because the source states that P2P payments and receipts cancel and are omitted from the optimisation; if so, reclassify the rule's applicability accordingly rather than requiring an invented payment equation.","If a mathematical settlement formula is required, provide explicit source-supported payment and receipt definitions, including buyer price application, seller receipt treatment, indices, and any loss/conversion adjustment. The supplied evidence does not justify inferring buyer payment = p_{p2p} * I or seller receipt = p_{p2p} * X for this rule.","Clarify whether Eq. (6) belongs only to the clearing objective rule R001, and whether its mention of omitted P2P terms is to be retained for R007 solely as evidence of cancellation rather than as an R007 objective expression."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
